3630a4e70a7f7373f5a31f740e96","event_uuid":"a069c5bd-98f2-4551-81d8-9a3bdb29f772","position":{"commit_sha":"ebd6aab2fea58d11f2e97b68e912e479d66ff22b","position":"1788771177056930001-a069c5bd-98f2-4551-81d8-9a3bdb29f772"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting execution: ticket is fully specified; running plan review before claim.","timestamp":1788746315839811001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review blocked on missing Acceptance Criteria, Testing, and file impact; added concrete AC/testing sections and declared expected file impact.","timestamp":1788746649696354001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review attempt still did not produce a passing attestation; skipping implementation per workflow.","timestamp":1788747147918500001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Amended plan before review to explicitly remove structured_output=False and update declare_no_file_impact no-schema/schema expectations, per prior review blocker.","timestamp":1788760508925029001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Skipped per workflow after amended plan review still BLOCKed. Verbatim blocking findings:\n\n1. The plan's premise that declare_no_file_impact can adopt 'the existing additive ack dict shape so it can include ok and optional cross_session_warning' is not backed by the code: the existing MCP write-ack shape (WriteAckOut, produced by _ack()) exposes a field named 'result' (whose value is 'ok'), not a field named 'ok'. No existing MCP write-ack model carries an 'ok' field (ok:bool exists only on the unrelated PlanReviewStatusOut/VerifyCompletionStatusOut read models at _mcp_models.py:499/510). The plan therefore both mis-describes an 'existing' shape and leaves ambiguous whether it means reuse WriteAckOut (field 'result') or introduce a new shape with an 'ok' field.\n\n2. The plan describes the additive ack for declare_no_file_impact as an object 'containing ok', but the existing shared ack shape (_ack -> WriteAckOut) exposes a field named 'result' (value 'ok'), not a field literally named 'ok'.\n\n3. The plan describes the declare_no_file_impact ack as 'the existing additive ack dict shape so it can include `ok`', but the existing shared ack (`_ack` -> `WriteAckOut`) exposes a field named `result` whose VALUE is 'ok' (plus push_status/description_warning/cross_session_warning) — there is no field literally named `ok`. The 'contains `ok`' wording could lead an implementer to invent a new `ok` field or write a test asserting an `ok` key, diverging from the reused shape.","timestamp":1788761125859324001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-remediated plan wording: replaced the ambiguous `ok` field wording with the exact existing `WriteAckOut` / `_ack()` contract: field `result` with value `\"ok\"`, plus optional `cross_session_warning`.","timestamp":1788770530345591001}],"created_at":1787889814329741001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"721683aa-a039-43f3-b666-31c28954c0a8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"734d-0998-c47c-48d9"}],"description":"Follow-up to the MCP cross-session warning story (734d). That story covers all single-ticket mutation tools plus `show_ticket`, including `transition_ticket`/`reopen_ticket` via an additive dict key. Three single-ticket tools remain deferred because their current return contracts do not yet carry the warning: `check_ac` and `quality_check` return `GateResultOut`, and `declare_no_file_impact` currently returns a bare string acknowledgement. Extend the cross-session warning to these three so the MCP structured-response surface matches the CLI warning behavior.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add optional `cross_session_warning: str | None = None` to the shared `GateResultOut` model so `check_ac` and `quality_check` can carry the same advisory field without changing their existing gate fields.\n- In `_mcp_reads.check_ac` and `_mcp_reads.quality_check`, compute the existing `_cross_session(ticket_id)` warning and attach it to the model returned from `rebar.check_ac` / `rebar.quality_check`.\n- Change `_mcp_writes.declare_no_file_impact` from a bare string ack to the existing `WriteAckOut` / `_ack()` additive ack shape so it can include `result: \"ok\"` plus optional `cross_session_warning`.\n- Remove the `structured_output=False` registration override from the `declare_no_file_impact` MCP tool; once the tool returns an object with a schema, it must participate in the normal structured output contract instead of advertising an unstructured string response.\n- Update the no-schema/schema expectations for `declare_no_file_impact`: tests that previously expected no output schema or a bare string acknowledgement must now expect the existing write-ack object schema with `result` constrained to the value `\"ok\"` and optional `cross_session_warning`.\n- Update the MCP cross-session tests and output-schema expectations so the structured response contract is explicit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py` so a ticket held by another session returns `cross_session_warning` from MCP `check_ac`, `quality_check`, and `declare_no_file_impact`; the test should fail before implementation because the first two lack the field and the third returns a string.\n- Extend the same test module's schema assertion so `GateResultOut` advertises optional `cross_session_warning`.\n- Update schema/coverage tests that intentionally encoded `declare_no_file_impact` as an unstructured string ack, including the no-schema/schema expectations.\n- Run targeted tests: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope_heldout.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] MCP `check_ac` returns the existing gate verdict fields plus optional `cross_session_warning`, checked by a unit test that exercises a cross-session claim.\n- [ ] MCP `quality_check` returns the existing gate verdict fields plus optional `cross_session_warning`, checked by a unit test that exercises a cross-session claim.\n- [ ] MCP `declare_no_file_impact` returns the existing additive `WriteAckOut` ack object containing `result: \"ok\"` and optional `cross_session_warning`, checked by a unit test that exercises a cross-session claim.\n- [ ] The `declare_no_file_impact` MCP registration no longer uses `structured_output=False`, and the MCP output schemas/schema coverage tests reflect the existing `WriteAckOut` fields (`result: \"ok\"`, optional warning fields) rather than the old no-schema/string expectation.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"add optional cross_session_warning to GateResultOut and expose ack model if needed"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"attach cross-session warning to check_ac and quality_check MCP outputs"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"return an additive ack object with cross_session_warning for declare_no_file_impact"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py","reason":"red/green tests for the remaining MCP cross-session warning tools and schemas"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py","reason":"update output-schema coverage for declare_no_file_impact ack shape"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope_heldout.py","reason":"update heldout MCP output-schema expectation for declare_no_file_impact"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c0341104-3fe2-49eb-84f2-8369785992aa","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"83aa-153e-4ff1-4300","ticket_type":"task","title":"MCP: carry cross_session_warning in dict/GateResult-returning single-ticket tools","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f660935b-637f-424d-93ff-b7de1b804bb5","f973fa93-0610-4913-bf16-a39893783f85","fce6754a-feed-4155-9ab0-27dd4846410f","99785a9a-4628-42d6-8edc-404b4dd3e792","6c723a22-11ca-41c0-a13f-7e4a70682e52","f016b419-18be-488f-ad1d-db804b7b41d8","915cf4f5-8284-45e8-8810-bdde998bb0dc","640d8cec-d79c-41ff-9d94-74ef8c948994","d3915b9e-96d6-4f00-a78f-410c12283614","bda78b79-a7a5-4d21-b3b7-9a1edc2da0fe","11857aed-e445-484c-bcd7-f8a6d378cfe8","c0341104-3fe2-49eb-84f2-8369785992aa","a069c5bd-98f2-4551-81d8-9a3bdb29f772"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788774894892357001,"uuid":"aa71a4c0-97e8-4032-8ccf-8b754898d361"}